{"step_index":65,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T20:14:11Z","content":"Now I have everything. Let me build the complete fine-tuning pipeline for **Fluxnat Coder 3B**.","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Complete implementation plan to fine-tune Qwen 2.5 Coder 3B Abliterated into 'Fluxnat Coder 3B' — a fully rebranded cybersecurity-focused coding model.\n\nCovers:\n1. 3-stage training pipeline: Stage 1 (Domain Pre-training on CyberSecurity-1M), Stage 2 (Instruction Tuning on CyberLLMInstruct + CTI datasets), Stage 3 (Chain-of-Thought Reasoning Distillation)\n2. Full rebranding: config.json, tokenizer_config.json, model card, system prompt, special tokens\n3. Two approaches: QLoRA via Unsloth (recommended, runs on free Colab T4) and Full Fine-Tuning (for 24GB+ GPUs)\n4. Complete project structure with all scripts\n5. Evaluation and benchmarking plan\n6. Publishing to HuggingFace as fluxnat/Fluxnat-Coder-3B","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# 🔥 Fluxnat Coder 3B — Complete Fine-Tuning & Rebranding Plan\n\n> Transform `Qwen 2.5 Coder 3B Abliterated` into your own **Fluxnat Coder 3B** — a fully rebranded, cybersecurity-specialized coding model.\n\n---\n\n## What We're Building\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| **Base Model** | `huihui-ai/Qwen2.5-Coder-3B-Instruct-abliterated` |\n| **Output Model** | `fluxnat/Fluxnat-Coder-3B` |\n| **Training Framework** | **Unsloth** (2x faster, 70% less VRAM) |\n| **Fine-Tuning Method** | QLoRA (4-bit) → Merge → Full model |\n| **Datasets** | CyberSecurity-1M + CyberLLMInstruct + CTI + custom |\n| **Training Hardware** | Free Google Colab T4 (16GB) or local GPU |\n| **Training Time** | ~4–8 hours on Colab T4 |\n\n---\n\n## Architecture: 3-Stage Training Pipeline\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    A[\"🏗️ Base Model\\nQwen 2.5 Coder 3B\\nAbliterated\"] --> B[\"Stage 1\\nDomain Pre-training\\nCyberSecurity-1M\"]\n    B --> C[\"Stage 2\\nInstruction Tuning\\nCyberLLMInstruct\\n+ CTI Dataset\"]\n    C --> D[\"Stage 3\\nCoT Reasoning\\nDistillation\"]\n    D --> E[\"🔥 Fluxnat Coder 3B\\nFully Rebranded\"]\n    E --> F[\"📦 Publish\\nHuggingFace Hub\"]\n```\n\n### Why 3 Stages?\n| Stage | Purpose | Dataset | What It Teaches |\n|-------|---------|---------|-----------------|\n| **Stage 1** | Domain knowledge injection | CyberSecurity-1M (~1M samples) | CVEs, threat intel, security concepts, attack patterns |\n| **Stage 2** | Task-specific instruction following | CyberLLMInstruct (~55K) + CTI (~20K) | \"Given this code, find the vulnerability and explain why\" |\n| **Stage 3** | Reasoning quality boost | Custom CoT dataset (~5K) | Step-by-step vulnerability reasoning chains |\n\n---\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nfluxnat-coder-3b/\n├── train.py                    # Main training script (Unsloth + QLoRA)\n├── prepare_datasets.py         # Download & format all datasets\n├── rebrand.py                  # Rename model → Fluxnat Coder 3B\n├── evaluate.py                 # Benchmark against base model\n├── merge_and_export.py         # Merge LoRA → full model → GGUF\n├── config/\n│   ├── training_config.yaml    # Hyperparameters\n│   └── model_card.md           # HuggingFace model card template\n├── data/\n│   ├── raw/                    # Downloaded datasets\n│   ├── processed/              # Formatted for training\n│   └── custom_cot/             # Hand-crafted CoT examples\n└── outputs/\n    ├── checkpoints/            # Training checkpoints\n    ├── merged/                 # Final merged model\n    └── gguf/                   # GGUF exports\n```\n\n---\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n### [NEW] `prepare_datasets.py`\n\nDownloads, cleans, and formats 3 cybersecurity datasets into Qwen chat format:\n\n```python\n# Datasets to combine:\n# 1. WhitzardAgent/CyberSecurity-1M        → Domain pre-training (~1M rows)\n# 2. CyberLLMInstruct                      → Instruction tuning (~55K rows)  \n# 3. soham-dahivalkar/cyber-threat-intelligence → CVE + MITRE ATT&CK (~20K rows)\n\n# Output format (Qwen chat template):\n{\n    \"messages\": [\n        {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are Fluxnat Coder, a cybersecurity AI...\"},\n        {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Analyze this code for SQL injection...\"},\n        {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"**Vulnerability Found: CWE-89 (SQL Injection)**\\n\\n**Step 1:** The user input `username` flows into...\\n**Step 2:** It is concatenated directly into...\\n**Step 3:** An attacker could inject...\\n\\n**Fix:**\\n```python\\ncursor.execute('SELECT * FROM users WHERE username=? AND password=?', (username, password))\\n```\"}\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### [NEW] `train.py` — Main Training Script\n\nFull training pipeline using **Unsloth** with QLoRA:\n\n```python\n# Key training decisions:\n# - Framework: Unsloth (2x faster, 70% less VRAM than vanilla HF)\n# - Method: QLoRA (4-bit base + LoRA adapters)\n# - LoRA rank: r=64 (high rank for deep domain adaptation)\n# - LoRA alpha: 128\n# - Target modules: ALL linear layers (q,k,v,o,gate,up,down projections)\n# - Learning rate: 2e-4 with cosine scheduler\n# - Batch size: 4 (gradient accumulation 4 = effective batch 16)\n# - Epochs: 3 per stage\n# - Max sequence length: 4096 tokens\n# - Warmup: 100 steps\n```\n\n**QLoRA config rationale:**\n- `r=64` (high) because we're doing a **deep domain shift** (general code → cybersecurity)\n- Target **all linear layers** for maximum adaptation\n- 4-bit quantization keeps VRAM at ~8GB (fits Colab T4)\n\n---\n\n### [NEW] `rebrand.py` — Complete Model Rebranding\n\nTransforms every trace of \"Qwen\" into **Fluxnat Coder 3B**:\n\n| File | What Changes |\n|------|-------------|\n| `config.json` | `name_or_path` → `fluxnat/Fluxnat-Coder-3B` |\n| `tokenizer_config.json` | `chat_template` → Fluxnat system prompt |\n| `special_tokens_map.json` | Keep compatible but update metadata |\n| `README.md` (Model Card) | Full Fluxnat branding, benchmarks, usage |\n| `generation_config.json` | Custom generation defaults |\n\n**System Prompt baked into the model:**\n```\nYou are Fluxnat Coder, a cybersecurity-specialized AI assistant created by Fluxnat. \nYou are an expert in vulnerability detection, code security analysis, penetration \ntesting, threat intelligence, and secure coding practices. You analyze code for \nsecurity flaws, explain vulnerabilities step-by-step, and provide actionable fixes.\n```\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **We keep `model_type: \"qwen2\"` in config.json** so the model stays compatible with all existing tools (HuggingFace, vLLM, llama.cpp). Only the branding changes — not the architecture identifier.\n\n---\n\n### [NEW] `merge_and_export.py`\n\nAfter training, merges LoRA adapters into the base model and exports:\n\n| Export Format | Use Case |\n|---------------|----------|\n| **HuggingFace (safetensors)** | Python inference, further fine-tuning |\n| **GGUF (Q4_K_M)** | llama.cpp, LM Studio, fast local inference |\n| **GGUF (Q8_0)** | Higher quality GGUF variant |\n\n---\n\n### [NEW] `evaluate.py`\n\nBenchmarks Fluxnat Coder 3B against the base model:\n\n| Benchmark | What It Tests |\n|-----------|--------------|\n| **CyberMetric** | Cybersecurity knowledge MCQs |\n| **SecBench** | Exploit prediction, vuln classification |\n| **HumanEval** | Code generation (ensure no regression) |\n| **Custom vuln samples** | Real vulnerable code detection accuracy |\n\n---\n\n### [NEW] `config/training_config.yaml`\n\n```yaml\n# Fluxnat Coder 3B Training Configuration\nmodel:\n  base: \"huihui-ai/Qwen2.5-Coder-3B-Instruct-abliterated\"\n  output_name: \"Fluxnat-Coder-3B\"\n  max_seq_length: 4096\n\nlora:\n  r: 64\n  alpha: 128\n  dropout: 0.05\n  target_modules:\n    - q_proj\n    - k_proj\n    - v_proj\n    - o_proj\n    - gate_proj\n    - up_proj\n    - down_proj\n\ntraining:\n  epochs: 3\n  batch_size: 4\n  gradient_accumulation: 4\n  learning_rate: 2e-4\n  scheduler: cosine\n  warmup_steps: 100\n  weight_decay: 0.01\n  fp16: true\n  load_in_4bit: true\n\ndatasets:\n  stage1:\n    name: \"WhitzardAgent/CyberSecurity-1M\"\n    max_samples: 100000  # Use 100K for stage 1\n  stage2:\n    - \"CyberLLMInstruct\"  # ~55K instruction pairs\n    - \"soham-dahivalkar/cyber-threat-intelligence\"  # ~20K CTI pairs\n  stage3:\n    name: \"custom_cot\"  # Hand-crafted chain-of-thought examples\n    path: \"data/custom_cot/\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Training Hardware Options\n\n| Option | GPU | VRAM | Cost | Time Est. |\n|--------|-----|------|------|-----------|\n| **Google Colab Free** | T4 | 16 GB | Free | ~6-8 hrs |\n| **Google Colab Pro** | A100 | 40 GB | \\$10/mo | ~2-3 hrs |\n| **Kaggle** | P100 / T4x2 | 16 GB | Free | ~6-8 hrs |\n| **Local RTX 3060** | 3060 | 12 GB | Own HW | ~8-10 hrs |\n| **Local RTX 4090** | 4090 | 24 GB | Own HW | ~1-2 hrs |\n| **RunPod / Vast.ai** | A100 | 80 GB | ~\\$1/hr | ~1 hr |\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Start with Google Colab Free (T4)** — Unsloth + QLoRA makes it totally feasible. You can train the entire Fluxnat Coder 3B on a free Colab notebook.\n\n---\n\n## Open Questions\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> 1. **Do you have a HuggingFace account?** Needed to download datasets and publish `fluxnat/Fluxnat-Coder-3B`.\n> 2. **Where will you train?** Google Colab (free), local GPU, or cloud rental?\n> 3. **Custom training data?** Do you have any of your own vulnerable code samples you'd like to include?\n> 4. **HuggingFace org name?** Should it be published as `fluxnat/Fluxnat-Coder-3B` or a different username?\n\n---\n\n## Build Order\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    S1[\"Step 1\\nprepare_datasets.py\\n📦 Download & format\"] --> S2[\"Step 2\\ntrain.py\\n🏋️ 3-stage training\"]\n    S2 --> S3[\"Step 3\\nmerge_and_export.py\\n🔗 Merge LoRA → full\"]\n    S3 --> S4[\"Step 4\\nrebrand.py\\n🎨 Rename to Fluxnat\"]\n    S4 --> S5[\"Step 5\\nevaluate.py\\n📊 Benchmark\"]\n    S5 --> S6[\"Step 6\\n🚀 Publish to\\nHuggingFace Hub\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## What Fluxnat Coder 3B Will Be Able To Do\n\n```\n🔍 \"Analyze this Python function for security vulnerabilities\"\n   → Identifies SQL injection, XSS, path traversal, etc.\n   → Explains the vulnerability chain step-by-step\n   → Provides a secure fix with code\n\n🛡️ \"What CWE does this vulnerability fall under?\"\n   → Maps to CWE-89, CWE-79, CWE-22, etc.\n   → Explains OWASP Top 10 category\n\n⚡ \"Generate a proof-of-concept exploit for this bug\"\n   → Creates PoC payloads (uncensored — no refusals)\n\n🔧 \"Rewrite this code to be secure\"\n   → Produces secure alternative with explanation\n\n📊 \"Rate the severity of this vulnerability\"\n   → CVSS-like scoring with detailed rationale\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Approve this plan and I'll start building all the scripts!** I'll create every file in the `fluxnat-coder-3b/` directory inside your project.\n","Description":"Complete plan to fine-tune and rebrand Qwen 2.5 Coder 3B into Fluxnat Coder 3B using Unsloth + QLoRA with cybersecurity datasets\"","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\k4ran\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\e2c1cf9f-2dff-4bf4-a974-ef410441acfa\\implementation_plan.md","toolAction":"Creating fine-tuning plan","toolSummary":"Fluxnat Coder 3B plan"}}]}
